# Cloudflare Pages redirects — 3locksmiths.co.il
#
# Ships in out/ from public/ (next build copies public/ wholesale; verified: out/_headers is
# byte-identical to public/_headers). wrangler auto-detects it at the root of the deploy dir —
# ops/deploy-site.ps1 does NOT special-case it, line 255 is a plain `npx wrangler pages deploy`.
#
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>. First match wins.
#
# ── THREE THINGS THAT MAKE A RULE HERE SILENTLY DO NOTHING ────────────────────
#
# 1. CASE. Matching is a case-SENSITIVE byte comparison of the percent-encoded request path.
#    This site emits LOWERCASE %d7% everywhere — sitemap.xml, every canonical, every authored
#    href — so lowercase is the form Google indexed and the form that must match. Uppercase is
#    what encodeURI() and most editors produce, and an uppercase-only rule set would be a 100%
#    no-op against every real URL. Both cases are listed below; the lowercase line is the one
#    that matters and the uppercase line is defence.
#
#    Do NOT copy the raw-Hebrew idiom from dalita.co.il/public/_redirects: Cloudflare normalises
#    a raw rule to UPPERCASE, so that file only matches uppercase requests and is half-broken
#    live today. Verified 2026-09-02 by curl against both siblings.
#
# 2. TRAILING SLASH. A rule written with a slash does not match a request without one. Today the
#    no-slash form 308s because the DIRECTORY exists in out/ — that 308 disappears the moment the
#    page is deleted, turning a working URL into a hard 404. Hence both forms for every path.
#
# 3. NO WILDCARDS UNDER /locations/. _redirects outranks existing static assets on Pages, so a
#    convenient `/locations/*` catch-all would black-hole all 25 surviving city pages. Exact
#    paths only. (410 is not expressible on Pages — only 301/302/303/307/308 — so 301 it is.)
#
# ── WHY THESE SEVEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Seven location pages withdrawn 2026-09-02 because the business no longer services those
# cities (docs/business-facts.md §E.1). באר שבע and ירושלים are original pre-migration
# WordPress permalinks holding real ranking signal, which is what CLAUDE.md golden rule 5 is
# about; the other five were generated by this project and are redirected too because they were
# live and in the sitemap.
#
# Target is the service-areas hub, not the homepage: a visitor who searched for a specific city
# can self-select one that is actually served, and the hub no longer claims the withdrawn ones.
# Not a nearest-city map — there is no honest substitute for ירושלים or באר שבע among the
# survivors, and Google treats a redirect to a non-equivalent page as a soft 404 anyway.
#
# VERIFY AFTER EVERY DEPLOY (the lowercase form is the one with no prior art anywhere in the
# fleet — if Cloudflare uppercase-normalises rules at parse time these lines are dead):
#   curl -sSI 'https://3locksmiths.co.il/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%9b%d7%a8%d7%9e%d7%99%d7%90%d7%9c/' | grep -iE 'HTTP/|location'
#   expect: HTTP/2 301  +  location: /%d7%90%d7%96%d7%95%d7%a8%d7%99-%d7%a9%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%95%d7%aa/

